ONTOLOGY_VERSION 0.1.0

STATUS DRAFT

OWNER President Cley Duarte

PURPOSE

Define the fundamental categories PACE reasons about, before any physical
representation exists. Four categories, deliberately kept separate:

Entities have identity independent of any single claim about them, persist
across time, and can be the subject or object of many independent relations
and assertions.

Relations connect two entities and carry no content of their own beyond the
connection and its type.

Assertions are claims of the form (subject, predicate, value, asserted_by,
as_of, version) attached to exactly one subject entity. An assertion has no
identity of its own — it is read, not cited.

Representation (file format, folder, naming convention) is excluded from
this document entirely. See contracts/ for how a given Contract version
chooses to represent these entities, relations and assertions physically.
A future representation change must never require changing this ontology.

ENTITY_TYPES

GOVERNED_UNIT

  A project or an organization — the same fundamental type. An
  organization is simply the root of a hierarchy of governed units, not a
  separate kind of thing.

  IDENTITY_FIELDS: NAME, SLUG, CREATED_AT

ACTOR

  Whoever asserts, decides, requests or approves — a person or an AI.
  Persists across many assertions and decisions; referenced by ID, never
  redefined per statement.

  IDENTITY_FIELDS: NAME, ROLE

  SCOPE: Defined once at the organization's own governed unit, referenced
  by ID from any project instance. Never duplicated per project.

DECISION

  An atomic recorded judgment. Citable — other entities point at a
  specific decision (a Release can say it implements Decision X; a later
  Decision can say it supersedes Decision Y).

  IDENTITY_FIELDS: ID, DATE

RELEASE

  An atomic record of a shipped artifact. Citable.

  IDENTITY_FIELDS: ID, DATE

REQUEST

  A pending, not-yet-crystallized ask, preference or rule. Has its own
  lifecycle (PENDING, PROMOTED, REJECTED, DEFERRED) and is referenced by
  whatever it becomes once resolved. The entry point of the future
  Engineering Requests Matrix / Knowledge Intake.

  IDENTITY_FIELDS: ID, DATE, STATUS

HISTORY_ENTRY

  A narrative record bundling several Decisions/Releases with
  interpretive context (why, alternatives discarded) that exists nowhere
  else. Citable, and itself cites other entities.

  IDENTITY_FIELDS: ID, DATE

RELATION_TYPES

BELONGS_TO
  BETWEEN GOVERNED_UNIT -> GOVERNED_UNIT
  MEANING A project belongs to an organization.

SUPERSEDES
  BETWEEN (a versioned assertion) -> (its previous version)
  MEANING Marks the chain of supersession without erasing history.

IS_CURRENTLY_ACTIVE
  BETWEEN GOVERNED_UNIT -> a specific version of an assertion sequence
  MEANING Which version is authoritative right now. Changing this is
  itself noteworthy enough to usually warrant a HISTORY_ENTRY.

DEPENDS_ON
  BETWEEN Component -> Component
  MEANING One component cannot be built or considered valid before
  another. Used at the PACE repository's own component level (see the
  separately-maintained Dependency Graph), not inside a project instance.

RESULTS_FROM
  BETWEEN RELEASE -> DECISION
  MEANING A shipped artifact traces back to the decision(s) that caused it.

PROMOTED_FROM
  BETWEEN DECISION | POLICY | PROTOCOL | STANDARD -> REQUEST
  MEANING Marks that a formal artifact originated from a specific,
  previously pending request.

CITES
  BETWEEN HISTORY_ENTRY -> DECISION | RELEASE
  MEANING A history entry narrates or references specific atomic records.

ASSERTED_BY / APPROVED_BY
  BETWEEN (any assertion or decision) -> ACTOR
  MEANING Who made the claim or approved the decision. Never a free-text
  label — always a reference to an ACTOR entity.

ASSERTION_TYPES

HAS_MISSION, HAS_VISION, HAS_ROADMAP, HAS_CURRENT_SPRINT
  SUBJECT GOVERNED_UNIT
  VALUE text content
  MUTABILITY superseded, never edited in place — every prior value stays
  NOTE Same assertion type at different points on one volatility
  spectrum: HAS_MISSION/HAS_VISION change rarely, HAS_ROADMAP
  occasionally, HAS_CURRENT_SPRINT often. Not four different kinds of
  knowledge — one kind, four subjects of attention, different churn rates.

HAS_NAME, HAS_SLUG, HAS_SCHEMA_VERSION, HAS_CREATED_AT
  SUBJECT GOVERNED_UNIT
  VALUE identity metadata
  MUTABILITY HAS_SCHEMA_VERSION changes as the instance migrates forward;
  the rest are permanent once set.

HAS_CONTINUITY_NOTE
  SUBJECT GOVERNED_UNIT or ACTOR
  VALUE informal accumulated fact or preference
  MUTABILITY refined in place, not versioned by discrete jumps — the one
  assertion type deliberately exempt from the supersession pattern above.

END
